{'page_ID': 8, 'quote_ID': 2, 'quote_text': "“A lady's imagination is very rapid; it jumps from admiration to love, from love to matrimony in a moment.”", 'quote_author': 'Jane Austen', 'quote_tags': ['humor', 'love', 'romantic', 'women']}
{'page_ID': 8, 'quote_ID': 3, 'quote_text': '“Remember, if the time should come when you have to make a choice between what is right and what is easy, remember what happened to a boy who was good, and kind, and brave, because he strayed across the path of Lord Voldemort. Remember Cedric Diggory.”', 'quote_author': 'J.K. Rowling', 'quote_tags': ['integrity']}
{'page_ID': 8, 'quote_ID': 4, 'quote_text': '“I declare after all there is no enjoyment like reading! How much sooner one tires of any thing than of a book! -- When I have a house of my own, I shall be miserable if I have not an excellent library.”', 'quote_author': 'Jane Austen', 'quote_tags': ['books', 'library', 'reading']}
{'page_ID': 8, 'quote_ID': 5, 'quote_text': '“There are few people whom I really love, and still fewer of whom I think well. The more I see of the world, the more am I dissatisfied with it; and every day confirms my belief of the inconsistency of all human characters, and of the little dependence that can be placed on the appearance of merit or sense.”', 'quote_author': 'Jane Austen', 'quote_tags': ['elizabeth-bennet', 'jane-austen']}
{'page_ID': 8, 'quote_ID': 6, 'quote_text': '“Some day you will be old enough to start reading fairy tales again.”', 'quote_author': 'C.S. Lewis', 'quote_tags': ['age', 'fairytales', 'growing-up']}
{'page_ID': 8, 'quote_ID': 7, 'quote_text': '“We are not necessarily doubting that God will do the best for us; we are wondering how painful the best will turn out to be.”', 'quote_author': 'C.S. Lewis', 'quote_tags': ['god']}
